Chapter: SamplerKernels
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 We say:

Section: Linear Combination

 out = a x + b y + c z over n f32 elements, one thread per element in blocks
 of 128; out may be x, y or z.

  kernel-lincomb3 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  kernel-lincomb3 (x) (y) (z) (out) (a) (b) (c) (n) = act
   bx <- block-idx-x
   bd <- block-dim-x
   tx <- thread-idx-x
   if bx * bd + tx < n then sk-lincomb-one x y z out a b c (bx * bd + tx) else 0
  end

  sk-lincomb-one : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  sk-lincomb-one (x) (y) (z) (out) (a) (b) (c) (i) = act
   xv <- device-load-f32 x i
   yv <- device-load-f32 y i
   zv <- device-load-f32 z i
   device-store-f32 out i (a * xv + b * yv + c * zv)
  end
